Found by lane-enum during B091, 2026-08-31, and deliberately NOT folded in --
the right call, because fixing it properly touches ~6 call sites and belongs to
every argument shape rather than to B091's rule.

## What it renders today

B091's fixture, line 44, an unwrapped method reference at an engine call:

    No matching signatures to 'startnew(void)'

`void` is the method's RETURN TYPE. It is printed where a callable belongs, so
the message names something that is not the argument and gives the author
nothing to act on -- the one thing they need is which callable shape was
expected and which they supplied.

## The same repo already does this correctly elsewhere

Declaration positions go through `render_func_or_type`, which renders the
SIGNATURE when the argument resolves to one:

    Can't implicitly convert from 'void()' to 'CoroutineFunc@'

That is the target quality. So this is not a design question -- it is one
renderer lagging another, and the good one is already written.

## Why it happens

`render_no_matching_sig` is given argument TYPES, not the argument expressions
or their resolved signatures, so by the time it renders there is nothing left
that could print `void()`. A callable has already been flattened to its return
type.

## The work

Thread the argument expressions (or their resolved `FuncdefSig`/function
signatures) into `render_no_matching_sig` at its ~6 call sites, and render a
callable argument as its signature -- reusing `render_func_or_type` rather than
writing a second renderer. A rule living at one of N sites is the recurring
defect shape in this repo (B073, B076, B098 were all instances).

Do it once for every argument shape, not bolted onto the funcdef-slot path:
the same flattening will mis-render any argument whose interesting property is
not its type.

## It is already pinned

B091's per-line tests assert the CURRENT text, so a later improvement shows up
as a deliberate test change rather than a silent one. Expect to update those
fixtures' expected output as part of this ticket; that is the design, not a
regression.

## Related

B091 (the fixtures and the pin), B025 (`this.Method` at funcdef ctor sites --
the declaration-position path that already renders well), B023 (the probe data
behind funcdef-slot rejection), B060 (a property READ is a value, not a
function -- another case where an argument's type is not the interesting fact
about it).